  "limitations": [
    "Visual system adaptation may have influenced results, potentially causing a centering bias, though this effect was considered minimal in the first stimulus range data.",
    "Instructions to avoid 'too bright' or 'too dim' conditions might have biased participants away from the extreme ends of the scale.",
    "Participants' knowledge of the proportional scale of options and the rate of change might have affected their settings.",
    "Variation in Correlated Colour Temperature (CCT) with dimming of halogen lamps could be a confound, although the estimated effect on preferred illuminance was small (<9.4%)."
  ],
